  ORDER CONTROL -- the identical ladder run both ways
    ascending  (-0.25 first)   up   +41.4   down  -284.3   asym -1.49
    descending (+0.25 first)   up  +287.6   down   -42.7   asym +1.48
    -> the asymmetry FLIPS SIGN with order: it is HYSTERESIS, and
       the SWEEP asymmetry is VOID. The static curve below is not
       affected -- it has no history to inherit.

  HYSTERESIS   mean |ascending - descending| at the same k = 107.1 Hz
  A controller must beat F1 jitter of sd 70-119 Hz. Backlash of the
  same order as the error gives a DEAD ZONE rather than convergence,
  so this number is a RESULT and not only a nuisance.

  STATIC CURVE -- a FRESH creature at every rung, no history
  k        F1 (Hz)            dF1 from 0
  -0.25       437.6 +/- 1.3     -192.2
  -0.18       464.6 +/- 0.8     -165.2
  -0.12       503.8 +/- 2.3     -125.9
  -0.06       562.0 +/- 4.8     -67.7
